{
  "name": "symbols_batch",
  "description": "USE WHEN: you need source (+ optionally direct callers/callees) for several EXACT qualified_names in one round trip — e.g. following up on a locate/search result list. Requires exact qualified_name, not a bare symbol name: an id that doesn't match exactly comes back found:false instead of fuzzy-substituting the closest name (unlike understand's fuzzy search). NOT FOR: a single bare-name lookup (use source/symbol_info) or exploring an unknown name (use search/locate first to get exact qualified_names). Capped at 50 ids per call.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "required": [
      "qualified_names"
    ],
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "qualified_names": {
        "description": "Exact `qualified_name`s to fetch (e.g. `path/to/file.rs::Type::method`)\n— NOT bare names. Get these from a prior `search`/`locate` call. This\ntool does no fuzzy matching: an id that doesn't match exactly comes\nback `found: false` for that entry rather than silently substituting\nthe closest name. Capped at 50 entries per call (extras are dropped,\nsee `truncated`).",
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "include_callers": {
        "description": "`true` to also include each found symbol's direct callers (same\nshape as `callers`'s `direct` field — no transitive/ambiguous split).",
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false
      },
      "include_callees": {
        "description": "`true` to also include each found symbol's direct callees.",
        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false
      }
    }
  },
  "outputSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "$defs": {
      "ErrorDetail": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "recoverable": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "review": {
            "description": "Wave 3: set only on `HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW` (the\ninitial refusal) and `DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH` (the refetch-and-retry\ncase) -- everything an agent needs to relay-approve/decline via\n`review_decide_via_agent_relay` without a separate read.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/PendingReviewPacket"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "next_call": {
            "description": "Wave 3: the exact next tool call this error implies, when there is\none unambiguous next step -- reuses `SuggestedNext` so a caller\nalready handling `suggested_next` elsewhere needs no new shape.\nBoxed (like `review` above) so this rarely-populated pair doesn't\ninflate every `ErrorDetail`/`Result<_, ErrorDetail>` on the hot,\ncommon path -- clippy's `result_large_err` flagged the unboxed form.",
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code",
          "message",
          "recoverable"
        ]
      },
      "PendingReviewPacket": {
        "description": "Wave 3 (audit follow-up, 2026-08-23): the structured shape of a\n`HIGH_RISK_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW`/`DIFF_DIGEST_MISMATCH` error's\n`review` field -- lets a calling agent relay-approve/decline without\never reading `pending_reviews` directly or reimplementing\n`hash_content` itself. `diff_digest` is always `hash_content(&diff_preview)`,\ncomputed server-side at the moment this packet is built -- never a\nvalue the caller supplied or guessed.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "review_id": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "diff_preview": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "diff_digest": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "expires_at": {
            "type": "number",
            "format": "double"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "review_id",
          "diff_preview",
          "diff_digest",
          "expires_at"
        ]
      },
      "SuggestedNext": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "tool": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "args": true,
          "gate": {
            "description": "Plan 3 §3.5(b): `Some(true)` iff skipping `tool` is actually\nhook-enforced (currently only the edit_context/edit_lines/edit_symbol\n→ diff_impact hints set this, via `suggested_gated`) — every other\nhint is left unset (`None`), meaning advisory-only. Lets an agent\ntell \"you'll be blocked if you skip this\" apart from \"you probably\nwant this next\" without re-deriving it from AGENTS.md prose each time.",
            "type": [
              "boolean",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "tool",
          "reason"
        ]
      },
      "SymbolsBatchEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "qualified_name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "found": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "kind": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "path": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "line_start": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "line_end": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "language": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "is_hub": {
            "type": [
              "boolean",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "source": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "token_estimate": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "content_warning": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "direct_callers": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CallerEntry"
            }
          },
          "direct_callees": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/CalleeEntry"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "qualified_name",
          "found"
        ]
      },
      "CallerEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "symbol": {
            "description": "`path::name` (or `path::Class::name`) — the enclosing file path is\nalways the substring before the first `::`, since every producer\n(tree-sitter extraction in `indexer::pipeline`, SQL indexer, SCIP\noverlay ingestion) derives both from the same `rel`/`from_path`\nvalue at the point the symbol/edge is created. A separate `path`\nfield used to duplicate this verbatim on every entry — pure waste\non a hub symbol with many callers in the same file; split on the\nfirst `::` if you need it standalone.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "edge_confidence": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "formal_source": {
            "description": "Nguồn cụ thể đứng sau `edge_confidence == \"formal\"`: `\"stack_graphs\"`\n(heuristic per-file — `resolver/formal.rs::FormalResolver::\nresolve_file` only ever sees ONE file at a time, no cross-module\nstitching) | `\"scip\"` (exact file,line, có thể cross-module) |\n`\"lsp\"` (runtime probe). `None` khi `edge_confidence != \"formal\"`,\nhoặc build thiếu mọi formal-tier feature. Không suy ra \"formal\" đáng\ntin bằng nhau — xem ADR-0002.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "edge_kind": {
            "description": "`\"call\"` or `\"reference\"` (SQL view/proc reading a table via\nFROM/JOIN) — see `call_edges.edge_kind`. Lets a consumer tell a real\ninvocation apart from a mere read without misreading a JOIN as a\nfunction call.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "preview": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "symbol",
          "edge_confidence",
          "edge_kind"
        ]
      },
      "CalleeEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "symbol": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "path": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "edge_confidence": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "formal_source": {
            "description": "See `CallerEntry::formal_source`.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "edge_kind": {
            "description": "See `CallerEntry::edge_kind`.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ],
            "format": "int64"
          },
          "preview": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "symbol",
          "path",
          "edge_confidence",
          "edge_kind"
        ]
      },
      "Caveat": {
        "description": "Structured, machine-checkable hint attached to a tool result whose\nliteral content (empty list / not-found) could otherwise be misread as\nproof of absence. `class` lets a safety gate branch without parsing\n`message`; `message` is the human-readable explanation. Design mirrors\nzzet/gortex's `ZeroEdgeCaveat` (Apache-2.0) — reimplemented against\nCALM's own resolver shape, not a line-for-line port.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "class": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "class",
          "message"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "flow_state"
    ],
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "flow_state": {
        "description": "Wave 11 (item 3, \"unified continuation state machine\"): present on\nevery response regardless of success/error -- `\"ready\"` on success,\nor one of `needs_context`/`needs_human_review`/`needs_verification`/\n`blocked` on error (see `classify_error_state`'s own doc comment).\nLets an agent dispatch on ONE top-level field instead of\nmaintaining its own per-`code` remediation table across ~70\ndistinct codes.\n\nNamed `flow_state`, not the more obvious `state` (audit follow-up,\n2026-08-23): several tool-specific success structs (e.g.\n`EditTransactionStatusOutput`, `VerifyChangeOutput` in txn.rs) have\ntheir own unrelated `state` field, and this struct's `success: T` is\n`#[serde(flatten)]`ed -- a same-named field there would silently\nserialize as a SECOND `\"state\"` JSON key (serde's flatten writes\neach field independently; nothing dedupes it), with most JSON\nparsers then last-write-wins-ing over whichever value serialized\nsecond. `flow_state` is deliberately namespaced so no domain output\nstruct will ever pick the same name by coincidence again.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "error": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ErrorDetail"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "results": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SymbolsBatchEntry"
        }
      },
      "found_count": {
        "type": "integer",
        "format": "uint",
        "minimum": 0
      },
      "not_found_count": {
        "type": "integer",
        "format": "uint",
        "minimum": 0
      },
      "truncated": {
        "description": "`true` when more than `SYMBOLS_BATCH_MAX` distinct ids were\nrequested — only the first `SYMBOLS_BATCH_MAX` (input order, after\ndedup) were looked up.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "caveat": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Caveat"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      },
      "suggested_next": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SuggestedNext"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "annotations": {
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false
  }
}
